  "description": "Protected brands for app/analysis/impersonation.py. Each entry names an app that fraudsters clone; the module flags APKs that wear a brand's package name, display name, or icon without being that brand's app.",
  "status": "SEED — package names and labels only. Every entry has verified=false because no icon hash or signing certificate has been recorded yet, and those two fields power the two strongest checks (icon reuse, certificate mismatch). Run scripts/build_brand_reference.py against real APKs to fill them in and flip verified.",
  "how_to_extend": "Do not hand-write icon_phash or cert_sha256 — both must come from a genuine APK obtained from the official listing, which is what scripts/build_brand_reference.py does. Adding a brand by package name alone still powers the typosquat and label checks.",
  "warning": "A WRONG package name here creates a false positive on the real app: the genuine bank APK would read as a typosquat of a package that does not exist. Verify each entry against the official store listing before relying on this table in a deployment.",
